# Task Group: Meizu 20 rooted USB contaminant-detection diagnosis and runtime workaround

scope: Live connected-device diagnosis and smallest reversible rooted sysfs change for a Meizu 20/Flyme USB contaminant warning that blocks charging; not a general moisture-bypass recipe.
applies_to: cwd=C:\Users\25011\Documents\codex\2026-11-01\wo; reuse_rule=device-, firmware-, root-method-, and runtime-specific: inspect the connected device and preserve/read back the original value before changing any sysfs control. Reboot persistence is unknown.

## Task 1: Diagnose and disable Meizu 20 USB contaminant detection, partial runtime success

### rollout_summary_files

- rollout_summaries/2026-10-31T19-18-06-hLD7-meizu20_root_disable_usb_moisture_detection.md (cwd=\\?\C:\Users\25011\Documents\codex\2026-11-01\wo, rollout_path=C:\Users\25011\.codex\sessions\2026\11\01\rollout-2026-11-01T03-18-06-01a19365-d557-7171-a2e8-cbfdb147e23d.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-31T19:33:24+00:00, thread_id=01a19365-d557-7171-a2e8-cbfdb147e23d, runtime change validated; reboot persistence unverified)

### keywords

- Meizu 20, Flyme 12.5.0.0A, meizu_20_CN, ADB, Magisk 28.1, /debug_ramdisk/su, moisture_detection_en, moisture_detection_status, contaminant_presence_status, UsbContaminantActivity, Charging

## User preferences

- when a phone is already connected over USB, the user corrected: "具体异常原因 你不能直接去看嘛，我已经用usb连接电脑了" -> inspect live host/ADB device state before asking for information that the connection can provide. [Task 1]
- when the user authorizes a rooted-device change, "我现在是已经给手机root了，还是没法解决吗，修改" -> verify root, preserve the original value, make the smallest targeted change, and validate the resulting hardware/software state. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- On this Meizu 20 / Flyme 12.5.0.0A build, the Qualcomm battery-driver controls were `/sys/class/qcom-battery/moisture_detection_en` (read/write enable) and `/sys/class/qcom-battery/moisture_detection_status` (status). Before the change, both were `1`, battery was `Not charging`, logs included `moisture: Contaminant presence detected`, and `dumpsys usb` reported `contaminant_presence_status=detected`. [Task 1]
- Ordinary `adb shell` was UID 2000; Magisk being installed was insufficient. `/debug_ramdisk/su -c id` returned `uid=0(root)` with `context=u:r:magisk:s0`, permitting the protected-node change. [Task 1]
- Writing `0` to `moisture_detection_en` yielded readback enable/status `0/0`, USB `contaminant_presence_status=not detected`, and battery `Not charging -> Charging`; the user confirmed "已经冲上电了". The prepared restoration script writes `1` through Magisk root and verifies its readback: `C:\Users\25011\Documents\codex\2026-11-01\wo\outputs\restore-meizu20-usb-detection.ps1`. [Task 1]
- This bypasses a hardware safety mechanism. Actual moisture or debris can create corrosion, heating, or damage risk; inspect/clean the port and restore protection after troubleshooting. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: `adb` is absent from PATH -> use official Platform-Tools and invoke its absolute `adb.exe`; this rollout used `work\android-diagnostic\platform-tools\adb.exe`. [Task 1]
- Symptom: ordinary shell cannot read/write the sysfs nodes -> explicitly verify `/debug_ramdisk/su -c id`; do not infer ADB root from Magisk UI presence. [Task 1]
- Symptom: nested PowerShell produces `Missing variable name after foreach` -> avoid fragile nested quoting; an encoded PowerShell command worked in this rollout. [Task 1]
- The setting was runtime-only and the device was not rebooted/reconnected because its battery was critically low. Do not claim boot persistence or a Magisk boot script: only a restoration script was created. [Task 1]


